## 📌 9. Complete Java Program

```java
class Animal {
}

class Dog extends Animal {
}

class Cat extends Animal {
}

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Object value = "Java";
        Animal pet = new Dog();
        Animal pet2 = new Cat();

        System.out.println(value instanceof String);
        System.out.println(value instanceof Integer);

        System.out.println(pet instanceof Dog);
        System.out.println(pet instanceof Animal);
        System.out.println(pet2 instanceof Cat);
        System.out.println(pet2 instanceof Dog);

        String name = null;
        System.out.println(name instanceof String);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
true
false
true
true
true
false
false
```

### Dry Run Table

| Expression | Explanation | Result |
|---|---|---|
| `value instanceof String` | `"Java"` is a String | `true` |
| `value instanceof Integer` | `"Java"` is not an Integer | `false` |
| `pet instanceof Dog` | The object is a Dog | `true` |
| `pet instanceof Animal` | Dog extends Animal | `true` |
| `pet2 instanceof Cat` | The object is a Cat | `true` |
| `pet2 instanceof Dog` | The object is not a Dog | `false` |
| `name instanceof String` | `name` is null | `false` |

